schema: "0.4"
id: fim-notebook-livebook-and-widgets-kino-datatable-04-edge-integration-state-accessibility
type: data
quality: high
solution: kino-datatable
category: notebook-livebook-and-widgets
variant: edge-integration-state-accessibility
prompt:
  system: |-
    You are a senior Elixir Livebook engineer. Output only one complete ASCII Elixir Livebook code cell for Kino.DataTable. No Markdown fences, no prose outside code. Prioritize validation, integration boundaries, and accessible table output.
  text: |-
    Create a Kino.DataTable edge/integration cell that accepts a simulated external query result or CSV-shaped rows without connecting to any external service. Validate expected columns, convert positional rows into named maps, normalize atom/string keys safely, and render a detail table plus a validation issues table. Include fallback demo data when the input is empty or malformed.

    Requirements: document Livebook/Kino compatibility; avoid database credentials and real network calls; handle heterogeneous rows, missing columns, duplicate keys, nils, and oversized input; pre-format dates, currency, and booleans for accessibility; include a note that richly styled or editable cells require Kino.JS; include safe execution checks for atom creation, row limits, and untrusted data.
  provider_options:
    max_tokens: 8192
    temperature: 0.2
    top_p: 0.9
output:
  text_format: elixir
  artifact_kind: livebook-kino-datatable-edge-cell
  formats:
  - format: exs
evaluation:
  checklist:
  - "Import check: generated code installs kino and uses Kino.DataTable.new/2 for detail and validation tables."
  - "Notebook compatibility: comments identify Livebook/Kino and explain integration boundaries without requiring external services."
  - "Reactive state: built-in table state handles sorting and pagination; validation state is explicit and deterministic."
  - "Data shape: positional rows are converted to maps, key normalization is bounded, malformed rows are reported, and fallback rows exist."
  - "Accessibility and fallback: validation messages, column names, formatted values, and fallback status are readable."
  - "Safe execution: no live database credentials, remote queries, unsafe atom creation, eval, shell commands, or unbounded row materialization."
  rubric:
  - name: Format validity
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Output is one complete ASCII Elixir Livebook code cell with no Markdown fences or explanatory wrapper."
    - "The code is valid and every table receives supported named-field data."
    - "The cell includes clear compatibility, fallback, and validation comments."
  - name: Semantic completeness
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Implements integration-shaped validation, positional-to-named conversion, detail rendering, and issue reporting."
    - "Uses current Kino.DataTable APIs and avoids unsupported editing, theming, or bare tuple assumptions."
    - "Includes notebook/livebook compatibility, reactive state, data shape, accessibility, fallback, and safe execution checks."
  - name: UX/structural quality
    weight: 25
    criteria:
    - "Validation issues and usable data are separated into clearly named tables."
    - "Column order and formatting make the edge cases easy to inspect."
    - "Fallback and error states are visible without relying on color."
  - name: Robustness
    weight: 15
    criteria:
    - "Handles empty, malformed, heterogeneous, oversized, duplicate, and nil-heavy input."
    - "Limits atom creation and keeps all sample data local and deterministic."
    - "Documents when to switch to Kino.JS or upstream sampling for richer or larger workflows."
  pass_conditions:
  - "All required YAML fields are present and the generated artifact is one valid ASCII Elixir Livebook cell."
  - "Rubric weights are exactly Format validity 30, Semantic completeness 30, UX/structural quality 25, Robustness 15."
  - "The prompt requires notebook/livebook compatibility, reactive state, data shape, accessibility, fallback, and safe execution checks."
  - "The solution remains Kino.DataTable-centered and treats integration data as validated local input."
tags:
- fim
- notebook-livebook-and-widgets
- livebook
- kino-datatable
- edge-integration-state-accessibility
